{"name":"Gossamer Wings","hex":"#e8eee9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gossamer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fine film made up of cobwebs, seen floating in the air or caught on bushes, etc.","A soft, sheer fabric."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tenuous, light, filmy or delicate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gossamer"},{"term":"wings","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of wing"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of scuba harness with an attached buoyancy compensation device: see wikipedia:Backplate and wing","A flip (hairstyle)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wings"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lycaenidae","blocks":[{"text":"Lycaenidae is a family of butterflies with over 6,000 species worldwide; its members are also called gossamer-winged butterflies. It is the second-largest butterfly family, constituting about 30% of the known butterfly species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Maculinea_arion_Large_Blue_Upperside_SFrance_2009-07-18.jpg/330px-Maculinea_arion_Large_Blue_Upperside_SFrance_2009-07-18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lycaenidae","wikidata":"Q158717"},{"title":"Wing","blocks":[{"text":"A wing is a structure which produces both lift and drag while moving through air. Wings are defined by two shape characteristics, an airfoil section and a planform. Wing efficiency is expressed as lift-to-drag ratio, which compares the benefit of lift with the air resistance of a given wing shape, as it flies. Aerodynamics includes the study of wing performance in air."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Wing.two.arp.600pix.jpg/330px-Wing.two.arp.600pix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wing","wikidata":"Q161358"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https